For our client, a premier global human and animal nutrition company we are looking for an IT Support Specialist_Production Environment, from Constanta or nearby.
 Main Responsibilities:
Identifying, diagnosing, and resolving hardware and software incidents, including Windows operating system issues and problems across a range of software applications;
Developing and maintaining strong client relationships to ensure a high level of customer service;
Installing, maintaining, and providing technical support for IT equipment (laptops, telecommunications equipment, printers, scanners, mobile devices, and workstations), as well as performing cabling and installation tasks;
Managing user accounts, access permissions, user rights, and security groups;
Setting up, maintaining, and supporting conference room equipment and meeting-related requests;
Configuring browsers and troubleshooting internet browser compatibility issues;
Identifying and resolving security-related issues affecting end-user devices;
Monitoring and verifying the successful execution of daily, weekly, and monthly backups;
Creating, maintaining, and publishing support documentation to facilitate the timely resolution of incidents and service requests and promote user self-sufficiency;
Assisting with the installation of network infrastructure, including LAN cables, network interface cards, and switches.
 The Ideal Candidate:
Minimum 2 years of equivalent IT Support in an Industrial Environment;
Experience with MS Office, Windows, AD, O365;
ITIL Foundation Certificate/ Project methodology is preferred;
Cloud technology experience;
Experience on Windows Imaging process using SCCM deployment;
Knowledge on Data Migration tools and O365 One drive;
Knowledge on ITIL and IT service management tool – Service Now;
Fluent English;
Driving license.
